# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
# An output leaves the run alone (#233) in double precision: in the
# deterministic mode the run with `[output] observables`, the free-energy
# file, the pull file, an energy file, and a trajectory ends in the state of
# the run without them, bit for bit, with the rows of its log, under NPT
# with the barostat of Trotter type on the CPU. The same with
# `rebuild_interval`, and for the rows of the log at the end only (D204). A
# Python simulation whose parts are read between them, or that has
# reporters, ends in the state of one that is not read.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/output_independence.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU mdir %t Double NPT-TROTTER | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: CPU Double NPT-TROTTER: {{[0-9]+}} builds of the neighbor structure in 40 steps
# CHECK-SAME: compared observables, free_energy, pull, files, interval-files, rows-at-end
# CHECK: CPU Double mdir run: the outputs leave the final state and the rows of the log as they are without them, in 1 ensembles
# CHECK: CPU Double Python: state() and view() between the parts and the reporters
# CHECK: output independence passed
